                <pb facs="0799" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1607c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-15T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1920—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>What is extent and influence of the authority exercised in Chinese Eastern
                    Railroad zone by Russian Consul over and above his functions as a Russian Consul
                    on Chinese territory and what are his official connections with the railroad?
                    What are his views as to (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Japanese (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Semenov (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) control
                    of the railroad?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
